      "text": "Heavy Rainfall Warning No. 3 #NCR_PRSD\nWeather System: Severe Tropical Storm OPONG\nIssued at: 8:00 AM, 26 September 2025(Friday)\n\nYELLOW WARNING LEVEL: Quezon(Mauban, Sampaloc, Lucban, Tayabas, Lucena, Pagbilao, Atimonan, Padre Burgos, Agdangan, Gumaca, Unisan, Plaridel, Macalelon, Pitogo, General Luna, Catanauan, Mulanay, San Andres, San Francisco, San Narciso, Buenavista, Guinayangan, Lopez, Calauag, Tagkawayan, Quezon, Alabat, Perez, Polillo, Panukulan, Patnanungan, Jomalig, Burdeos).\nASSOCIATED HAZARD: FLOODING in flood-prone areas.\nMeanwhile, expect light to moderate rains over Zambales, Bataan, Tarlac, Pampanga, Nueva Ecija and Bulacan within the next 3 hours.\nLight to moderate with occasional heavy rains affecting Cavite, Metro Manila, Rizal, Batangas, Laguna and Quezon(Candelaria, Dolores, San Antonio, Sariaya, Tiaong, General Nakar, Infanta, Real) which may persist within 3 hours.\n\nThe public and the Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Offices concerned are advised to MONITOR the weather condition and watch for the next warning to be issued at 11:00 AM today.\nFor more information and queries, please call telephone numbers 8927-1335 and 8927-2877 or log on to https://t.co/59mTpZJq1n.",
